n: BoxDecoration(\n                          color: palette.fgPrimary\n                              .withValues(alpha: config.dotOpacity),\n                          shape: BoxShape.circle,\n                        ),\n                      );\n                    },\n                  ),\n                ),\n              ),\n              // Optional song-info overlay pinned to the top of the hero band (B-020), above the dot.\n              if (config.showSongInfo)\n                Positioned(\n                  left: 0,\n                  right: 0,\n                  top: 12,\n                  child: Opacity(\n                    opacity: config.textOpacity.clamp(0.0, 1.0),\n                    child: HeroTitleBlock(textScale: config.textScale),\n                  ),\n                ),\n            ],\n          ),\n        );\n      },\n    );\n  }\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787220258801}}},{"sequence":8529,"timestamp":"2026-08-20T10:04:21.395326Z","elapsed_seconds":577.691,"source":"pi","event":{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_FDn6nNz44jRIALt3fIYdu1tR|fc_0e2eb0930c8b9c68016a86d121ef588195b8b60c56d7f3b501","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import 'dart:math';\n\nimport 'package:flutter/material.dart';\nimport 'package:provider/provider.dart';\n\nimport '../../models/screen_config.dart';\nimport '../../services/playback_controller.dart';\nimport '../../theme/app_palette.dart';\nimport '../../theme/app_typography.dart';\nimport 'base_hero_container.dart';\nimport 'hero_title_block.dart';\n\n/// Dot visualisation embedded in the Void hero slot: a single pulsing circle whose radius tracks the spectrum's bass energy (Void chrome owns transport). When [DotScreenConfig.showSongInfo] is true (B-020) the active track's Artist (H1) / Song (H2) overlay the top of the band in a [Stack] above the centered dot, using the shared [HeroTitleBlock] (B-046). The dot is clamped to a fraction of the smallest dimension so it never overflows.\nclass DotHero extends StatelessWidget {\n  const DotHero({super.key, required this.config});\n\n  final DotScreenConfig config;\n\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    final palette = Theme.of(context).extension<AppPalette>()!;\n    // read (not watch): the dot animates off [spectrumListenable] below, so this\n    // widget must NOT rebuild on every controller notify.\n    final player = context.read<PlaybackController>();\n\n    return LayoutBuilder(\n      builder: (context, constraints) {\n        final maxAllowed = min(constraints.maxWidth, constraints.maxHeight) / 2;\n        return BaseHeroContainer(\n          child: Stack(\n            children: [\n              // Pulsing dot \u2014 always centered. Only this subtree repaints per\n              // spectrum frame (RepaintBoundary-isolated).\n              Center(\n                child: RepaintBoundary(\n                  child: AnimatedBuilder(\n                    animation: player.spectrumListenable,\n                    builder: (context, _) {\n                      final r = _radiusFor(player.spectrumData, maxAllowed);\n                      return Container(\n                        width: r * 2,\n                        height: r * 2,\n                        decoration: BoxDecoration(\n                          color: palette.fgPrimary\n                              .withValues(alpha: config.dotOpacity),\n                          shape: BoxShape.circle,\n                        ),\n                      );\n                    },\n                  ),\n                ),\n              ),\n              // Optional song-info overlay pinned to the top of the hero band (B-020), above the dot.\n              if (config.showSongInfo)\n                Positioned(\n                  left: 0,\n                  right: 0,\n                  top: 12,\n                  child: Opacity(\n                    opacity: config.textOpacity.clamp(0.0, 1.0),\n                    child: HeroTitleBlock(textScale: config.textScale),\n                  ),\n                ),\n            ],\n          ),\n        );\n      },\n    );\n  }\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787220258801}}},{"sequence":8530,"timestamp":"2026-08-20T10:04:21.525492Z","elapsed_seconds":577.821,"source":"pi","event":{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Editing code methods**\n\nI noticed that we removed the `_radius` for the old block, but I didn't insert the new one. It seems like I need to edit it again to add the complete new method and make all the necessary modifications. So, I'll open the file to correctly patch that up. There\u2019s definitely some clarity needed here, and I want to ensure everything is sorted out properly. Let\u2019s get to it!","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0e2eb0930c8b9c68016a86d11ea1cc8195a018df20d6f4eea3\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABqhtEhgQEGbx5Y7yRXAukruFHIZlMe-FsHK2J6oN8aLgjgymfrKfZe5RO3UFvRjp5Z5Aq6Jej3PkcCdXrHd-g_8HKL4nLy7ZZLB_zdkIPmBPFNK52GbZxrTzSPmIAobVlHj8WyeWfraxZOJtQP6S0gem54CESUA3xCX1qTj6FA8xTxyh1Qj7eEpZuqaYygwpXe9LDG2MrAKW_EO2QPKcuKj3N9VxCpv8Ti3oZ5qux6BQCUg-qmTh7hbkZsbz-bXv-hkD63TDH9QK1nTRC7dyMHYfRic6G5eb4nkhJn3HkQJ_706DhW20KtGBg3H2X5SfiI13haRTZTFrJpfi8EE5dsT4wFpZfTXvA0CiMDGIjxXF8etM3slBTUsxDTEGZUQ_9q9w787s3KXhw4nwwjfEx8maBC8p-Y0BK16SSWvYxfAQ7TAUCxVrdPBSCgFgUm9OiKMzarTpxvEgyHjsIP_efsTrkDomMLs__Kk4mwwYoAoYf6mhcz44la0SZDWylTpDMjJ_MEcWoLbSTEUatequtU5kHH4dWm4GEGCiG_JLLq_8s6W7LBpoLML8M9q7_LTQn2O9CFhiFw7WYUp_fsKRnri2mUC63W2wfLdcb4l7SlL_3kp4huevhVOVIOfdGTCm2jbIuC17E1acwYecHuIP_jo5bBNvrYAJZ0vGcf1I97cBTMxGWJSue_PYAOKZ_X6MC2ysK8RUI0V7rq-T0U6ZEKRREamat11jiCzZMeBdsgjNfwDR47-HEN5VOwdtMS_Q5m2BWBQGmFXQCWjF5wPAFRGRigf-E59-o0YV3k3YYX1E_um4FhuUrF83l5e5MG3_MFRE5ovwEyja5lkRnlvd8cAOfqfEvsh-jLTUdpL0AsrdWz90KNw_HUGUFPoxoiY9hxNPX5hz3oSCD261Mwz0AqxLC0Y3atTMioj8ZKaR-NG8MMM9Od9sc0tnGvMTDAfUmq_wy18kbUYILD9mBpCnaKNOAuZAZekDnOlBC3sEwDEdKPwaw3t